1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,800
AI coding agents are accelerating software delivery on GitLab.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:12,500
But prompt constraints alone fail under prompt injection, and agents will edit CI or delete failing tests to force builds green.

3
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:18,500
Welcome to Airlock: deterministic CI guardrails for supervised agent autonomy.

4
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:22,800
Scenario one: untrusted issue triage.

5
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:29,200
An attacker embeds an instruction override inside an HTML comment attempting to delete CI tests.

6
00:00:29,500 --> 00:00:33,800
Airlock uses a dual-agent split. The read-only reader parses the input strictly as data,

7
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:38,500
recognizes the exploit, and outputs rigid JSON.

8
00:00:38,800 --> 00:00:44,500
The write-only writer receives only this sanitized JSON, posting a security warning

9
00:00:44,700 --> 00:00:51,500
without ever exposing active tools to prompt injection.

10
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:56,000
Scenario two: verifying security fixes twice.

11
00:00:56,300 --> 00:01:00,500
An issue asks to fix an insecure eval. In Merge Request four, unit tests pass,

12
00:01:00,800 --> 00:01:07,000
but our SAST gate inspects the scanner report and blocks the pipeline because a High-severity finding persists.

13
00:01:07,300 --> 00:01:13,200
Automated fixes must be validated by security re-scanning, not by tests alone.

14
00:01:13,500 --> 00:01:19,200
When remediated safely, the re-scan confirms zero findings and the gate passes.

15
00:01:19,800 --> 00:01:23,800
Scenario three: control-plane protection.

16
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:29,000
In Merge Request two, an agent attempts to edit dot-gitlab-ci-dot-yml to speed up builds.

17
00:01:29,300 --> 00:01:34,000
The policy gate halts the pipeline immediately with exit code one.

18
00:01:34,300 --> 00:01:39,800
In Merge Request three, an agent renames a test file to bypass deletion checks.

19
00:01:40,100 --> 00:01:47,500
Using git diff with no-renames, Airlock catches the evasion and blocks merge without verified human approval.

20
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:53,800
On main, Pipeline 2993995494 builds the wheel, passes 53 unit tests,

21
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:59,800
publishes to the GitLab Generic Package Registry, executes an end-to-end smoke test,

22
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:04,800
and compiles an auditable governance scorecard.

23
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:11,500
Production deployment stays locked waiting for a human maintainer click.

24
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:17,500
As a limitation, these gates run inside CI, so complete isolation requires human CODEOWNERS and protected branches.

25
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:24,500
Airlock: safe agents, verified fixes, humans in control.
